# EXAMPLES

The devices on QEMU's x86_64 machine, some of them, and devmgr starting the RTC's driver:

```text
bus-acpi: \_SB.PCI0 PNP0A08 io=0xcf8/8
bus-acpi: \_SB.PCI0.SF8.KBD PNP0303 io=0x60/1 io=0x64/1 irq=1
bus-acpi: \_SB.PCI0.SF8.COM1 PNP0501 io=0x3f8/8 irq=4
bus-acpi: \_SB.PCI0.SF8.RTC PNP0B00 io=0x70/8 irq=8
devmgr: \_SB.PCI0.SF8.RTC PNP0B00: /boot/bin/drv-rtc-cmos
bus-acpi: 38 devices, 29 present with a hardware ID; 273 KiB of heap
```

Two of the probe's requests, refused, then the AML's first touches, granted:

```text
devmgr: bus-acpi refused memory 0xfee00000/4096
devmgr: bus-acpi refused I/O ports 0x3f8/8
devmgr: bus-acpi gets I/O ports 0x604/2
devmgr: bus-acpi gets PCI configuration 0xf8/4096
```

On aarch64, where the UART is memory:

```text
bus-acpi: \_SB.COM0 ARMH0011 mem=0x9000000/0x1000 irq=33
bus-acpi: 52 devices, 47 present with a hardware ID; 162 KiB of heap
bus-acpi: serving /srv/acpi
```

# FILES

: `/srv/acpi`
  The post `bus-acpi` serves: power off.
: `/boot/bin/bus-acpi`
  The program, which devmgr reads from bootfs.
: `/boot/svc/devmgr.ndb`
  devmgr's manifest, whose `claim=acpi` is the post.

